From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:37:53 +0000
Subject: Show no icon on the browser start screen

Since Android 12 the system shows a start screen whenever the browser
starts without a running process. By default that screen shows the app
icon in the middle of the screen until the browser draws its first
frame. The browser already sets the background of that screen to the
color of its surface. Set the icon to a transparent drawable as well, so
the screen is a plain area of that color and the browser's own toolbar
replaces it.

Only the theme of the tabbed browser changes. Custom tabs and installed
web apps keep their own start behavior. Android 11 and older show no
start screen icon and are not affected.

License: GPL-2.0-or-later - https://spdx.org/licenses/GPL-2.0-or-later.html
---
 chrome/android/java/res/values/styles.xml | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/android/java/res/values/styles.xml b/chrome/android/java/res/values/styles.xml
--- a/chrome/android/java/res/values/styles.xml
+++ b/chrome/android/java/res/values/styles.xml
@@ -66,6 +66,8 @@ found in the LICENSE file.
     <style name="Base.Theme.Chromium.TabbedMode" parent="Theme.Chromium.WithWindowAnimation">
         <item name="android:statusBarColor">@macro/default_bg_color</item>
         <item name="android:windowLightStatusBar">@bool/window_light_status_bar</item>
+        <!-- The start screen shows only its background color, without the app icon. -->
+        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon" tools:targetApi="31">@android:color/transparent</item>
     </style>
     <style name="Theme.Chromium.TabbedMode" parent="Base.Theme.Chromium.TabbedMode"/>
 
